Package: carbonite
Title: A Carbon Design System Toolkit for Shiny
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Evan", "Brand", , "etbrand@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Encapsulate your Shiny applications in the IBM Carbon Design 
    System using high-performance web components. By leveraging the 
    '@carbon/web-components' library, 'carbonite' allows developers to 
    build enterprise-grade, accessible, and high-performance user 
    interfaces without writing custom CSS or complex JavaScript. Designed 
    for developers who need a reliable and professional aesthetic, the 
    package includes a suite of atomic components and complex layout 
    structures such as data tables and side-navigation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/etbrand/carbonite
BugReports: https://github.com/etbrand/carbonite/issues
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    cli,
    htmltools (>= 0.5.2),
    rlang,
    shiny (>= 1.5.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Suggests: 
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
